WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.100
Paris, 28 December 1895.

2
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:11.220
The Lumière brothers charge the
public to watch moving pictures.

3
00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.170
It is the first public,

4
00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:12.850
paid film screening.

5
00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:16.330
Today the French have a
grand name for cinema:

6
00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:17.210
«le septième art».

7
00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:18.520
Seventh? Then which six arts come first,

8
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:21.360
and why would cinema
earn a place beside them?

9
00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.970
In this mission, you'll follow
a timeline from the Lumière

10
00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:27.990
brothers to «la Nouvelle
Vague» and the «Palme d'or».

11
00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.890
Then you'll find out how
France pays for its films,

12
00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:32.550
and why it calls them culture,

13
00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.050
not just goods: «l'exception culturelle».

14
00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:38.700
Your mission: work out why
cinema is number seven,

15
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.670
and what keeps French films alive.
